  @media (min-width: 768px) { .ex-status { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
  .ex-card { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem; background: #fff; }
  .ex-card h3 { font-weight: 600; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .ex-card p { font-size: 1rem; }
  .ex-timeline { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0.25rem 0 0; }
  .ex-timeline li { position: relative; padding: 0 0 0.8rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.98rem; color: #374151; }
  .ex-timeline li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0.2rem; top: 0.5rem; width: 0.45rem; height: 0.45rem; border-radius: 999px; background: #d1d5db; }
  .ex-timeline li:last-child::before { background: var(--accent); }
  .ex-timeline li::after { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0.39rem; top: 1rem; bottom: -0.1rem; width: 1px; background: var(--line); }
  .ex-timeline li:last-child::after { display: none; }
  .ex-timeline span { font-family: "Source Code Pro", ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); margin-right: 0.4rem; }

  .ex-term { background: var(--night); color: #e5e7eb; border-radius: 1rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem; font-family: "Source Code Pro", ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.8; overflow-x: auto; }
  .ex-term .p { color: #6b7280; user-select: none; }
  .ex-term .c { color: #6b7280; }

  .ex-cli { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.98rem; }
  .ex-cli td { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0.6rem 0.5rem 0.6rem 0; vertical-align: top; color: #374151; }
  .ex-cli td:first-child { white-space: nowrap; padding-right: 1.25rem; }

  .ex-not { display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 640px) { .ex-not { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .ex-not div { background: var(--soft); border-radius: 0.8rem; padding: 0.85rem 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: #374151; }
  .ex-not b { display: block; color: var(--ink); }

  /* Uses */
  .ex-uses { display: grid; gap: 1px; background: var(--line); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; overflow: hidden; }
  @media (min-width: 640px) { .ex-uses { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .ex-use { background: #fff; padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem; }
  .ex-use h3 { font-family: var(--font-source-serif-pro); font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .ex-use p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .ex-use em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent-ink); }
</style>

<article class="ex max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-8 pt-24 pb-24">
  <a href="/projects/" class="text-sm text-gray-500 hover:text-black transition-colors">← All projects</a>

  <header class="mt-8">
    <p class="ex-kicker">{% for tag in project.tagLinks %}<a href="{{ tag.url }}" class="hover:text-black transition-colors">{{ tag.label }}</a> · {% endfor %}{{ project.years }}</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl font-medium tracking-tight mt-3">{{ project.title }}</h1>
    <p class="ex-lede mt-4 max-w-2xl">See your Claude Code and Codex sessions in one place: what each one said and what it cost. For Claude Code, agent calls appear as a live tree, so you can see who called whom and whether each one is still working.</p>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-7">
      <a class="ex-btn primary" href="https://github.com/unwind-labs/unwind" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View on GitHub</a>
      <a class="ex-btn" href="https://pypi.org/project/unwind-labs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pip install unwind-labs</a>
      <a class="ex-btn" href="/projects/callstack/">Companion project: callstack</a>
    </div>

    <dl class="ex-meta mt-10">
      <div><dt>Status</dt><dd><span class="ex-dot"></span>Stable</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Latest release</dt><dd>0.5.0 · October 2026</dd></div>
      <div><dt>License</dt><dd>MIT, open source</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Runs on</dt><dd>Your machine, Python 3.11+</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <figure class="mt-10">
      <button type="button" data-zoom class="ex-shot cursor-zoom-in" aria-label="Expand the unwind session view">
        <img src="/images/projects/unwind/hero.png" alt="unwind showing a list of Claude Code sessions on the left and a call tree on the right, with subagents, calls, and the cost of each branch" width="2932" height="1756" decoding="async">
      </button>
      <figcaption class="ex-caption mt-3">One session, four helpers. Two subagents and one call are complete; the last call is still working. Each card shows its own cost.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </header>

  <!-- 01 Why -->
  <section class="ex-section" id="why">
    <div class="ex-section-head"><span class="ex-num">01</span><h2 class="ex-h2">Why I built it</h2></div>
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p>I built unwind for two reasons. The first was a practical need: I couldn't see what my other project, callstack, was doing. The second was curiosity about cost.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ex-reasons">
      <div class="ex-reason">
        <p class="ex-kicker">Reason 1</p>
        <h3 class="ex-h3">I needed to see callstack's call trees</h3>
        <p>I was building <a class="ex-link" href="/projects/callstack/">callstack</a>, which lets Claude Code call another full Claude Code session the way a program calls a function. That session does a big piece of work and returns its result. It can also call sessions of its own, so a single task can grow into a deep tree of calls. Claude Code showed all of these as one flat list of sessions. I wanted to see the tree.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-reason">
        <p class="ex-kicker">Reason 2</p>
        <h3 class="ex-h3">How much am I really using?</h3>
        <p>I was paying $200 a month for my Claude subscription. I'd heard that subscriptions give you far more in tokens than you pay for, and I wanted to know if that was true for me. It was. Every month I was using billions of tokens, worth thousands of dollars at API prices.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-2xl mt-8">
      <h3 class="ex-h3">The idea behind callstack</h3>
      <p>Subagents usually work in parallel and send results back loosely, so the agent that started them can miss something. callstack brings the discipline of function calls to agents instead. Each call runs to completion, its result comes back in a predictable way, and the caller collects every result before it moves on. Calls can nest as deep as the work needs, so full Claude Code sessions can take on large, complex tasks together. At the time, Claude Code had nothing like this.</p>
      <p>unwind made callstack visible. I could watch calls appear as they were made and check that they behaved correctly: which calls were running, which had started calls of their own, which were waiting for their children, and which had finished.</p>
      <h3 class="ex-h3 mt-8">Later: Codex too</h3>
      <p>I also started using OpenAI's Codex heavily, often on the same projects as Claude Code. I didn't want to check two places, so I added Codex support. Since version 0.5.0, unwind shows Claude Code and Codex sessions for a project together.</p>
    </div>

    <aside class="ex-name">
      <p class="ex-kicker">Why "unwind"?</p>
      <p>When the functions in a call stack finish and return their results one by one, the stack <em>unwinds</em>. That's the link to callstack. The word also means to relax, and I like that the name carries both meanings.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 What it does -->
  <section class="ex-section" id="what">
    <div class="ex-section-head"><span class="ex-num">02</span><h2 class="ex-h2">What it does</h2></div>
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p>Run <code>unwind serve</code> in any project folder, and unwind opens a browser view of every Claude Code and Codex session that ran there, including months of history. Sessions started by callstack calls appear nested under the session that called them, not as a flat list. You don't install hooks or change how you use either tool.</p>
      <p>For Codex sessions, unwind shows messages, tool calls, reasoning summaries, and token cost. Call trees and live status are available for Claude Code sessions.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ex-flow" aria-label="How unwind fits together">
      <div class="ex-col">
        <div class="ex-node"><b>Claude Code session logs</b><small>Conversations, tool calls, and token use. Already on your machine.</small></div>
        <div class="ex-node"><b>Codex session logs</b><small>Messages, tool calls, and token use, shown alongside Claude Code sessions.</small></div>
        <div class="ex-node"><b>callstack call logs</b><small>Optional. Adds nested calls between agents.</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ex-node core"><b>unwind</b><small>Joins them into one tree and prices each turn at the model that produced it</small></div>
      <div class="ex-arrow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ex-col">
        <div class="ex-node"><b>Web view</b><small>Session list, call-tree canvas, conversation detail, monthly report.</small></div>
        <div class="ex-node"><b>Command line</b><small>The same data as text or JSON, for scripts and for agents.</small></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ex-caption">Everything stays on your computer. unwind sends no data anywhere.</p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <div class="ex-feature">
        <div>
          <span class="ex-tag" style="background:#ede9fe;color:#5b21b6">Call tree</span>
          <h3 class="ex-h3">The whole multi-agent run as one tree</h3>
          <p>Subagents and callstack calls appear as connected cards, nested to any depth. Select any card to read that agent's conversation.</p>
          <div class="ex-legend"><span><i style="background:#7c3aed"></i>Subagent</span><span><i style="background:#0ea5e9"></i>Call with shared context</span><span><i style="background:#10b981"></i>Call with fresh context</span></div>
        </div>
        <button type="button" data-zoom class="ex-shot cursor-zoom-in" aria-label="Expand the call tree screenshot">
          <img src="/images/projects/unwind/call-tree.png" alt="A call tree with a root session, two subagents, and several nested calls, each with its own cost" width="2082" height="1544" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-feature flip">
        <div>
          <span class="ex-tag" style="background:#d1fae5;color:#065f46">Live status and cost</span>
          <h3 class="ex-h3">Know at a glance if it's busy, stuck, or done</h3>
          <p>New calls appear as they're made. Each card shows whether the call is running, has started calls of its own, is waiting for its children, or has finished. If an agent is waiting on you, that shows up all the way back to the root. Every card also shows what that session spent and what its whole branch spent.</p>
          <div class="ex-legend"><span><i style="background:#10b981"></i>Working or complete</span><span><i style="background:#d97706"></i>Waiting on you</span></div>
        </div>
        <button type="button" data-zoom class="ex-shot cursor-zoom-in" aria-label="Expand the live session screenshot">
          <img src="/images/projects/unwind/hero.png" alt="A running session with completed helpers marked done and one call still in progress" width="2932" height="1756" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-feature">
        <div>
          <span class="ex-tag" style="background:#e0f2fe;color:#075985">Conversation detail</span>
          <h3 class="ex-h3">Read any agent's conversation</h3>
          <p>Open a session to see each message, tool call, and reasoning step in order, with helpers nested where they started. It's the fastest way to find out why an agent stalled or failed.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" data-zoom class="ex-shot cursor-zoom-in" aria-label="Expand the conversation detail screenshot">
          <img src="/images/projects/unwind/node-detail.png" alt="A session's conversation with the user request, tool calls, and a nested subagent" width="2932" height="1756" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="ex-feature flip">
        <div>
          <span class="ex-tag" style="background:#fef3c7;color:#92400e">Usage report</span>
          <h3 class="ex-h3">Monthly spend across every project</h3>
          <p>This is the question that started unwind. The Reports view, or <code>unwind usage report</code>, shows a month's total tokens and their cost, then breaks both down by project. You can see Claude Code and Codex together or one at a time. Costs are estimates at each provider's API prices, which makes it easy to see what your subscription is really worth.</p>
        </div>
        <button type="button" data-zoom class="ex-shot cursor-zoom-in" aria-label="Expand the usage report screenshot">
          <img src="/images/projects/unwind/usage-report.png" alt="A monthly usage report with total cost, tokens, sessions, projects, and a per-project breakdown" width="2932" height="1756" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03 Status -->
  <section class="ex-section" id="status">
    <div class="ex-section-head"><span class="ex-num">03</span><h2 class="ex-h2">Status</h2></div>
    <div class="ex-status">
      <div class="ex-card">
        <h3>Where it stands</h3>
        <p>unwind is stable and free to use. I built the first version in about six weeks in spring 2026 and shipped 18 releases to PyPI along the way. Version 0.5.0, released in October 2026, added Codex support.</p>
        <p>It's now in maintenance. It does what I built it to do, so I'm not planning major new features. I'll keep it working as Claude Code and Codex change.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ex-card">
        <h3>Timeline</h3>
        <ul class="ex-timeline">
          <li><span>Apr 2026</span>First public release, 0.1.0</li>
          <li><span>May 2026</span>0.2 to 0.4: twelve releases in four weeks</li>
          <li><span>Jun 2026</span>0.4.5, the last release before Codex support</li>
          <li><span>Oct 2026</span>0.5.0 adds Codex sessions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 Get it -->
  <section class="ex-section" id="get-it">
    <div class="ex-section-head"><span class="ex-num">04</span><h2 class="ex-h2">Open source and how to try it</h2></div>
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p>unwind is open source under the MIT license. The code is on <a class="ex-link" href="https://github.com/unwind-labs/unwind" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>, and the package is on <a class="ex-link" href="https://pypi.org/project/unwind-labs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PyPI</a>. You need Python 3.11 or later and a project you've used with Claude Code or Codex.</p>
    </div>
    <pre class="ex-term mt-6"><span class="p">$ </span>pip install unwind-labs
<span class="p">$ </span>cd path/to/your/project
<span class="p">$ </span>unwind serve   <span class="c"># opens the view in your browser</span></pre>

    <table class="ex-cli">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>unwind project</code></td><td>List and find the projects unwind knows about.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>unwind session</code></td><td>List sessions in a project, inspect one, or print its tree.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>unwind messages</code></td><td>Print or search a session's messages.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>unwind task</code></td><td>Explore the combined tree of calls and subagents.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="ex-caption mt-3">Add <code>--harness claude</code> or <code>--harness codex</code> to list sessions from one tool.</p>

    <div class="ex-not">
      <div><b>Local only</b>Your sessions never leave your machine.</div>
      <div><b>No setup</b>No hooks, plugins, or startup scripts in Claude Code or Codex.</div>
      <div><b>Read only</b>unwind never changes your agents or their logs.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 Uses -->
  <section class="ex-section" id="uses">
    <div class="ex-section-head"><span class="ex-num">05</span><h2 class="ex-h2">What you can use it for</h2></div>
    <div class="ex-uses">
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>Find the branch that blew the budget</h3><p>When a run costs more than expected, follow the costs down the tree to the agent that spent it.</p></div>
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>Check on long runs</h3><p>See whether a run that's taking a while is busy, stuck, or <em>waiting on you</em>, without scrolling through a transcript.</p></div>
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>See what your subscription is worth</h3><p>Find out how many tokens you use each month, what they would cost at API prices, and which projects use the most.</p></div>
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>Let Claude Code search its own history</h3><p>Every command can return JSON, so Claude Code can use unwind as a tool. Ask it to summarize what the last subagent did, or to find the earlier session where you solved the same bug.</p></div>
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>Debug multi-agent workflows</h3><p>If you build with subagents or callstack, see how a run actually branched and read exactly what each agent was told.</p></div>
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>Use Claude Code and Codex side by side</h3><p>If you switch between both on the same project, see all their sessions in one list.</p></div>
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>Explain agent runs to others</h3><p>Export the tree as an image to show a team how a multi-agent run unfolded.</p></div>
      <div class="ex-use"><h3>Build your own deep call stacks</h3><p>Pair unwind with callstack to try nested agent calls and watch every level run.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>
